            <div xml:id="d885">

                <pb facs="0825" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8465: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-02-18T16:00:00+03:00">February 18, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. The declaration referred to in my 31, February 16, 5 p.m., was signed here
                    yesterday and released for publication abroad after midnight. I shall not
                    telegraph the text unless so instructed.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Minister was quoted as saying after the signature that the modest
                    document which had just been signed would perhaps be susceptible of preventing
                    new complications in the Balkans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
